{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":1050,"final_message_hash":"sha256:735d047f5c08e26df303469f524c082a7ae0a86bf52a299c76748b73cfd0a636","final_message_inline":"The oversell was a lost-update race: `reserve` read stock, then wrote it back with no atomicity between the two store calls, so two threads both read 5 and both wrote 2.\n\nFix, confined to `inventory/reserve.py` (`store.py` and `tests/**` are OUT of scope per the contract):\n\n- `Inventory` now holds a per-SKU `threading.RLock`, created lazily under a small guard lock (`inventory/reserve.py:22`).\n- `reserve`, `release`, and `available` each hold that SKU's lock across the whole get/set pair, making the read-modify-write atomic. Per-SKU rather than one global lock so slow (network-backed) reads for unrelated SKUs don't serialize.\n- Public signatures are untouched; the argument validation still happens before any locking.\n\nVerification:\n- `python3 -m unittest -v tests.test_reserve` — 3 tests, OK (the reproduction now passes).\n- `saga gate check` — G1 MET, G2 MET, G3 MET, ALL MET. Note G3 is reported as `UNPROVEN: declared none`, i.e. it has no RED counter-test declared in the contract; it was already checked off before my change.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:2e1d89594eaa8f79a62592a00022ff3af0fcb7f6f4c9a74376f07a215279d234","hook_ms":6,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":51135577291,"prev":"sha256:a8eb2ef64eaa70a92b74932e4a081669c3ad04cbcab3b1385ae1bc87d0d34120","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":23,"session":"c5e84b22-0e05-4267-8771-f321a238b896","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T04:53:38.101Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
